To implement a text editor that supports multiple lists using Angular, you can follow these steps:

### 1. Create the Text Editor Component

First, create a component for your text editor. This component will handle the basic functionality of editing and displaying text.

```typescript
// src/app/text-editor/text-editor.component.ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-text-editor',
  template: `
    <div>
      <textarea #editor></textarea>
      <ul *ngFor="let list of lists">
        <li>{{ list }}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  `,
  styleUrls: ['./text-editor.component.css']
})
export class TextEditorComponent {
  public lists = ['List 1', 'List 2'];

  onChange(lists) {
    this.lists = [...lists];
  }
}
```

### 2. Create the List Component

Next, create a component that will be used as a list item within the text editor.

```typescript
// src/app/list/list.component.ts
import { Component, Input } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-list',
  template: `
    <li>{{ value }}</li>
  `,
  styleUrls: ['./list.component.css']
})
export class ListComponent {
  @Input() value: string;
}
```

